    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1343">

                <pb facs="1150" n="1046" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1046"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/571b.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                            Brown Brothers and Company.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-08-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 20, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Kindly telegraph the amount now owed you by Nicaragua, and send by mail the terms
                    and conditions on which you would increase your <pb facs="1151" n="1047"
                        xml:id="pg1047"/> loan for about one year to between $2,000,000 and
                    $2,500,000; also state whether you would consider your security on the latter
                    amount ample without option on the railroad.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
